.TH V7CC 1 "August 2026" "V7 toolchain" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
v7cc \- V7 PDP-11 C compiler driver (host-ported)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B v7cc
[ option ] ... file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I v7cc
is the Seventh Edition Unix C compiler driver, run host-side as a
cross-compiler for the PDP-11.  It strings together the preprocessor,
the two compiler passes, the optional peephole optimizer, the assembler
and the linker.
.PP
Arguments whose names end in
.B .c
are C source; they are compiled, each leaving a
.B .o
file (deleted if a single program is compiled and loaded in one step).
Arguments ending in
.B .s
are assembly source, assembled to
.BR .o .
Other arguments are loader options or C-compatible object files or
libraries, loaded (in order) into
.BR a.out .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-c
Suppress the load phase; produce a
.B .o
file even for a single program.
.TP
.B \-S
Compile and leave the assembler output on the corresponding
.B .s
file.
.TP
.B \-P
Run only the preprocessor, leaving a
.B .i
file with no
.B #
lines.
.TP
.B \-E
Run only the preprocessor, sending the result to standard output.
.TP
.B \-O
Invoke the peephole optimizer (
.BR v7c2 ).
.TP
.B \-p
Produce profiling code (counts calls); link the profiling startup
.RB ( mcrt0.o ).
.TP
.B \-f
Use the floating-point variant (links the floating-point interpreter).
.TP
.BI \-o " output"
Name the final output file
.IR output .
.TP
.BI \-D " name=def"
Define
.I name
to the preprocessor as if by
.BR #define .
.TP
.BI \-U " name"
Remove any initial definition of
.IR name .
.TP
.BI \-I " dir"
Search
.I dir
for
.B #include
files.
.TP
.BI \-B " string"
Find the substitute compiler passes in the files named
.I string
with the suffixes
.BR c0 ,
.BR c1 ,
.BR c2
and
.BR cpp .
.TP
.BR \-t [ p012 ]
Find only the designated passes.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B V7_CPP V7_C0 V7_C1 V7_C2 V7_AS V7_LD
Full paths to the individual passes; these override the compiled-in
defaults (used to point at a build tree before install).
.TP
.B V7_CRT0 V7_LIB
The startup object and the target library directory, respectively.
.SH FILES
.ta \w'/usr/local/lib/pdp11-v7/  'u
file.c	input file
.br
file.o	object file
.br
a.out	loaded output
.br
/tmp/ctm?	temporaries
.br
/usr/local/bin/v7cpp	preprocessor
.br
/usr/local/bin/v7c0 /usr/local/bin/v7c1	compiler passes
.br
/usr/local/bin/v7c2	peephole optimizer
.br
/usr/local/bin/v7as /usr/local/bin/v7as2	assembler
.br
/usr/local/bin/v7ld	loader
.br
/usr/local/lib/pdp11-v7/crt0.o	runtime startoff
.br
/usr/local/lib/pdp11-v7/libc.a	standard library
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IR v7as (1),
.IR v7ld (1),
.IR v7cpp (1),
.IR v7c2 (1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Diagnostics from the C passes are intended to be self-explanatory;
occasional messages may come from the assembler or loader.
.SH BUGS
Linking is not yet wired end-to-end: the PDP-11
.B libc.a
must be present in
.BR /usr/local/lib/pdp11-v7
for a full
.B v7cc file.c
link; compile (
.BR \-c )
and assemble (
.BR \-S )
are self-contained.
